{"created_commit":"97c2daa5d445e57110fa64baa690e64934a6373a","created_generation":"GT-G0","epistemic_layer":"OBSERVATION","evidence_refs":["gravity-time/reports/round-g0-tables.json","gravity-time/reports/gt-g0-g1-report.md"],"finding_id":"GT-F01-DENS-NULL","literal_value":{"max_gap":4.5e-13},"magnitude_class":"zero_within_floor","notes":"Predicted by the autonomous factorisation CL-T18/CL-T19 of the Constraint Laboratory catalogue.","observable":"attachment fraction; triangles given edge count","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":5,"exactness":5,"parameter_robustness":4,"projection_robustness":4,"replication":5},"scope":"GT Round G0: N=5,6, HELD and FREE, label-covariant O=2 templates, exact kernels","statement":"The density template DENS leaves the density-controlled attachment fraction exactly at null and triangles given edge count exactly at the uniform conditional law, under both clocks (gaps below 5e-13).","status":"active","structural_roles":["negative_finding","bias"],"temporal_character":"stationary"}
{"created_commit":"97c2daa5d445e57110fa64baa690e64934a6373a","created_generation":"GT-G0","epistemic_layer":"OBSERVATION","evidence_refs":["gravity-time/reports/round-g0-tables.json","gravity-time/reports/gt-g0-g1-report.md"],"finding_id":"GT-F02-INCIDENCE-SELECTIVITY","literal_value":{"close_weak_n5":[0.8601,0.8571],"hold_strong_n5_clustering_k3":2.638},"magnitude_class":"small","notes":"Partly answers CL-Q04: these pair-coupled templates break autonomous factorisation.","observable":"attachment fraction and clustering","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":5,"exactness":5,"parameter_robustness":3,"projection_robustness":3,"replication":5},"scope":"GT Round G0: N=5,6, HELD and FREE, label-covariant O=2 templates, exact kernels","statement":"ADJ, CLOSE and HOLD raise the density-controlled attachment fraction above null under both clocks; CLOSE and HOLD raise triangles given edge count up to 2.6 times the uniform law in FREE mode. Margins shrink toward null at strong grades as the graph saturates.","status":"active","structural_roles":["bias","occupancy_shift"],"temporal_character":"stationary"}
{"created_commit":"97c2daa5d445e57110fa64baa690e64934a6373a","created_generation":"GT-G0","epistemic_layer":"METHODOLOGICAL","evidence_refs":["gravity-time/reports/round-g0-tables.json","gravity-time/reports/gt-g0-g1-report.md"],"finding_id":"GT-F03-DRIFT-CRITERION-CONFOUNDED","literal_value":null,"magnitude_class":"not_applicable","notes":"Recorded, not tuned after the fact.","observable":"frozen criterion behaviour","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":4,"exactness":5,"parameter_robustness":4,"projection_robustness":3,"replication":5},"scope":"GT Round G0: N=5,6, HELD and FREE, label-covariant O=2 templates, exact kernels","statement":"The frozen G0 inward-drift criterion does not separate attraction from density: DENS passes it by densification, and continuous-time drift scales with total rate. The frozen basin labels rest on the attachment criterion.","status":"active","structural_roles":["methodological_correction","negative_finding"],"temporal_character":"not_applicable"}
{"created_commit":"97c2daa5d445e57110fa64baa690e64934a6373a","created_generation":"GT-G0","epistemic_layer":"OBSERVATION","evidence_refs":["gravity-time/reports/round-g0-tables.json","gravity-time/reports/gt-g0-g1-report.md"],"finding_id":"GT-F04-RETENTION-NOT-APPROACH","literal_value":{"hold_ct_shell2":-3.0,"null_ct_shell2":-3.0},"magnitude_class":"not_applicable","notes":"","observable":"radial drift by clock","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":4,"exactness":5,"parameter_robustness":3,"projection_robustness":3,"replication":4},"scope":"GT Round G0: N=5,6, HELD and FREE, label-covariant O=2 templates, exact kernels","statement":"Under the continuous clock HOLD's frontier drift equals NULL's exactly at N=5; its jump-clock inward drift is normalisation. Soft admissibility makes a basin by reduced escape, not by approach.","status":"active","structural_roles":["support_boundary","normalisation_effect"],"temporal_character":"stationary"}
{"created_commit":"97c2daa5d445e57110fa64baa690e64934a6373a","created_generation":"GT-G0","epistemic_layer":"OBSERVATION","evidence_refs":["gravity-time/reports/round-g0-tables.json","gravity-time/reports/gt-g0-g1-report.md"],"finding_id":"GT-F05-RELATIONAL-POTENTIAL","literal_value":{"max_gap":8.7e-15},"magnitude_class":"not_applicable","notes":"Post-hoc reading of G0, verified on fresh kernels and by a fixture test; the standard detailed-balance (exponential random graph) construction.","observable":"pi_ct against m^S/Z","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":4,"exactness":5,"parameter_robustness":5,"projection_robustness":3,"replication":4},"scope":"GT Round G0: N=5,6, HELD and FREE, label-covariant O=2 templates, exact kernels","statement":"For every template the continuous-time stationary law is m^S/Z with S the edge count (DENS), wedge count (ADJ) or triangle count (CLOSE, and HOLD with m replaced by 1/m), within 9e-15 at N=5 in both modes. CLOSE(m) and HOLD(1/m) share one stationary law.","status":"active","structural_roles":["equivalence","normalisation_effect"],"temporal_character":"stationary"}
{"created_commit":"97c2daa5d445e57110fa64baa690e64934a6373a","created_generation":"GT-G0","epistemic_layer":"OBSERVATION","evidence_refs":["gravity-time/reports/round-g0-tables.json","gravity-time/reports/gt-g0-g1-report.md"],"finding_id":"GT-F06-LOCK-ARREST","literal_value":{"expected_steps":{"FREE5":15.23,"FREE6":20.5,"HELD5":8.86,"HELD6":14.64}},"magnitude_class":"not_applicable","notes":"Capture and total arrest, not a stationary basin.","observable":"absorption","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":4,"exactness":5,"parameter_robustness":3,"projection_robustness":3,"replication":5},"scope":"GT Round G0: N=5,6, HELD and FREE, label-covariant O=2 templates, exact kernels","statement":"LOCK is certainly absorbed into the complete graph, where no event is admissible, after 8.9 to 20.5 expected events.","status":"active","structural_roles":["support_boundary"],"temporal_character":"persistent"}
{"created_commit":"3dccd0a3f0e5227ef7e373d1aada7d01f6fcfba9","created_generation":"GT-G1","epistemic_layer":"OBSERVATION","evidence_refs":["gravity-time/reports/round-g1-tables.json","gravity-time/reports/gt-g0-g1-report.md"],"finding_id":"GT-F07-SHARED-BASIN-DIFFERENT-CLOCKS","literal_value":{"n5_strong":[0.637,0.039],"n6_strong":[0.262,0.011]},"magnitude_class":"large","notes":"Frozen predictions P1 and P3 hold.","observable":"near/far activity ratio","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":4,"exactness":5,"parameter_robustness":3,"projection_robustness":3,"replication":5},"scope":"GT Round G1: N=5,6, HELD, exact kernels, jump and continuous clocks","statement":"CLOSE(m) and HOLD(1/m) have identical continuous-time shell masses (gap 0) and different jump-clock shell masses (gap 0.0009 to 0.063). At one shared law their continuous-time near/far activity ratios are 0.637 and 0.039 (N=5 strong) and 0.262 and 0.011 (N=6 strong).","status":"active","structural_roles":["equivalence","negative_finding"],"temporal_character":"stationary"}
{"created_commit":"3dccd0a3f0e5227ef7e373d1aada7d01f6fcfba9","created_generation":"GT-G1","epistemic_layer":"OBSERVATION","evidence_refs":["gravity-time/reports/round-g1-tables.json","gravity-time/reports/gt-g0-g1-report.md"],"finding_id":"GT-F08-NEAR-SOURCE-SLOWING","literal_value":{"p2_cells_holding":1},"magnitude_class":"moderate","notes":"","observable":"near/far activity ratio","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":3,"exactness":5,"parameter_robustness":3,"projection_robustness":3,"replication":5},"scope":"GT Round G1: N=5,6, HELD, exact kernels, jump and continuous clocks","statement":"The near/far activity ratio is below 1 in 16 of 16 non-null cells under the jump clock and 15 of 16 under the continuous clock, including the density control; the exception is CLOSE weak at N=5 (1.034). Frozen prediction P2 (CLOSE above null, HOLD below) holds in 1 of 4 cells.","status":"active","structural_roles":["bias","negative_finding"],"temporal_character":"stationary"}
{"created_commit":"97c2daa5d445e57110fa64baa690e64934a6373a","created_generation":"GT-G0","epistemic_layer":"INFERENCE","evidence_refs":["gravity-time/reports/gt-g0-g1-report.md"],"finding_id":"GT-F09-POTENTIAL-AS-MECHANISM","literal_value":null,"magnitude_class":"not_applicable","notes":"","observable":"mechanism of basin formation","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":4,"exactness":4,"parameter_robustness":3,"projection_robustness":2,"replication":4},"scope":"GT Round G0: N=5,6, HELD and FREE, label-covariant O=2 templates, exact kernels","statement":"In the existing grammar a basin around a held relational structure arises from minimal label-covariant templates as occupancy of a relational potential (a motif count); the held structure is attractive because of how it enters the counted motif, with no rule naming a centre or direction.","status":"active","structural_roles":["bias","expressiveness"],"temporal_character":"stationary"}
{"created_commit":"3dccd0a3f0e5227ef7e373d1aada7d01f6fcfba9","created_generation":"GT-G1","epistemic_layer":"INFERENCE","evidence_refs":["gravity-time/reports/gt-g0-g1-report.md"],"finding_id":"GT-F10-KINETICS-NOT-POTENTIAL","literal_value":null,"magnitude_class":"not_applicable","notes":"","observable":"relation between basin and recurrence rate","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":3,"exactness":4,"parameter_robustness":3,"projection_robustness":2,"replication":4},"scope":"GT Round G1: N=5,6, HELD, exact kernels, jump and continuous clocks","statement":"Near-source slowing of local activity accompanies every basin tested, density included, as an occupancy effect; its size is set by kinetics, not by the stationary potential. H-U holds in a weak form and is contradicted in the strong form within this grammar.","status":"active","structural_roles":["interaction","negative_finding"],"temporal_character":"stationary"}
{"created_commit":"3dccd0a3f0e5227ef7e373d1aada7d01f6fcfba9","created_generation":"GT-G1","epistemic_layer":"RS_GLOBAL_COHERENCE_INTERPRETATION","evidence_refs":["gravity-time/reports/gt-g0-g1-report.md"],"finding_id":"GT-F11-RS-POTENTIAL-AND-CLOCK","literal_value":null,"magnitude_class":"not_applicable","notes":"Not a claim about physical gravity, nature's use of these templates, or the design premise.","observable":"interpretation","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":1,"exactness":2,"parameter_robustness":2,"projection_robustness":1,"replication":2},"scope":"GT G0-G1; not a claim about physical systems","statement":"Inside this model, relational primacy yields basins as potentials without a primitive centre, and the admissibility/tendency distinction separates capture, retention and approach. Any RS reading of gravitational clock-rate differences as relational would need a further principle tying kinetics to potential, which the current grammar does not supply.","status":"active","structural_roles":["expressiveness"],"temporal_character":"not_applicable"}
{"created_commit":"3dccd0a3f0e5227ef7e373d1aada7d01f6fcfba9","created_generation":"GT-G1","epistemic_layer":"OPEN_QUESTION","evidence_refs":["gravity-time/reports/gt-g0-g1-report.md"],"finding_id":"GT-Q01-KINETIC-CONVENTION","literal_value":null,"magnitude_class":"not_applicable","notes":"","observable":"rate as a function of potential","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":0,"exactness":0,"parameter_robustness":0,"projection_robustness":0,"replication":0},"scope":"GT Round G1: N=5,6, HELD, exact kernels, jump and continuous clocks","statement":"Is there a principled kinetic convention under which local recurrence rate is a function of the relational potential alone, and what would justify it?","status":"unresolved","structural_roles":["open_question"],"temporal_character":"unknown"}
{"created_commit":"3dccd0a3f0e5227ef7e373d1aada7d01f6fcfba9","created_generation":"GT-G1","epistemic_layer":"OPEN_QUESTION","evidence_refs":["gravity-time/reports/gt-g0-g1-report.md"],"finding_id":"GT-Q02-RADIAL","literal_value":null,"magnitude_class":"not_applicable","notes":"","observable":"radial dependence","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":0,"exactness":0,"parameter_robustness":0,"projection_robustness":0,"replication":0},"scope":"GT Round G1: N=5,6, HELD, exact kernels, jump and continuous clocks","statement":"Does attachment or activity have a stable dependence on relational distance across several shells (N=7, validated vectorised kernel)?","status":"unresolved","structural_roles":["open_question"],"temporal_character":"unknown"}
{"created_commit":"3dccd0a3f0e5227ef7e373d1aada7d01f6fcfba9","created_generation":"GT-G1","epistemic_layer":"OPEN_QUESTION","evidence_refs":["gravity-time/reports/gt-g0-g1-report.md"],"finding_id":"GT-Q03-SOURCE-DEPENDENCE","literal_value":null,"magnitude_class":"not_applicable","notes":"","observable":"source dependence","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":0,"exactness":0,"parameter_robustness":0,"projection_robustness":0,"replication":0},"scope":"GT Round G1: N=5,6, HELD, exact kernels, jump and continuous clocks","statement":"Does basin depth depend on the held structure's motif content (triangle, 4-clique, path)?","status":"unresolved","structural_roles":["open_question"],"temporal_character":"unknown"}
{"created_commit":"3dccd0a3f0e5227ef7e373d1aada7d01f6fcfba9","created_generation":"GT-G1","epistemic_layer":"OPEN_QUESTION","evidence_refs":["gravity-time/reports/gt-g0-g1-report.md"],"finding_id":"GT-Q04-ARREST-AND-SUCCESSION","literal_value":null,"magnitude_class":"not_applicable","notes":"","observable":"arrest","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":0,"exactness":0,"parameter_robustness":0,"projection_robustness":0,"replication":0},"scope":"GT Round G0: N=5,6, HELD and FREE, label-covariant O=2 templates, exact kernels","statement":"Does total admissibility arrest bear on the open candidate of a limit on primitive event succession?","status":"unresolved","structural_roles":["open_question"],"temporal_character":"unknown"}
{"created_commit":"c31ef92aaf6e5299b9cb15bd7b5c10e768d65f43","created_generation":"GT-E0A","dependence":{"clock":"law is the continuous-time law","parameters":"all W4 grades","projection":"none","scaffold":"holds HELD and FREE"},"epistemic_layer":"INFERENCE","evidence_refs":["gravity-time/reports/round-e0a-tables.json","gravity-time/reports/gt-e0a-reflection.md"],"finding_id":"GT-F12-SINGLE-WITNESS-REVERSIBLE","literal_value":{"cells":32,"max_irreversible_flux":6.5e-14},"magnitude_class":"not_applicable","notes":"Derived in gravity-time/docs/e0-coverage-and-selection.md section 3 before E0A; generalises GT-F05. Standard Kolmogorov / ERGM result applied to the grammar. Bears on CL-T18/CL-T19 (factorisation) and CL-Q04.","observable":"reversibility and stationary law","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":5,"exactness":5,"parameter_robustness":5,"projection_robustness":5,"replication":5},"scope":"GT Round E0A: N=5,6, HELD and FREE, label-covariant O=2 templates incl. two-witness PATH, exact kernels","statement":"Every label-covariant single-witness template composition on the O=2 pair grammar (form or dissolve, any sign, hard formation exclusion, HELD scaffold) is reversible with a triple-local Gibbs law exp(theta.(E,W,T)); verified exactly on 32 gradient cells (flux <= 6.5e-14, predicted-law L1 <= 1e-9).","status":"active","structural_roles":["equivalence","expressiveness"],"temporal_character":"stationary"}
{"created_commit":"c31ef92aaf6e5299b9cb15bd7b5c10e768d65f43","created_generation":"GT-E0A","dependence":{"clock":"flux fraction clock-free; sigma per event and per time both reported","parameters":"weak grade only","projection":"full state","scaffold":"present in HELD and FREE"},"epistemic_layer":"OBSERVATION","evidence_refs":["gravity-time/reports/round-e0a-tables.json","gravity-time/reports/gt-e0a-reflection.md"],"finding_id":"GT-F13-NONGRADIENT-ARROW","literal_value":{"flux_range":[0.088,0.158],"sigma_per_event_range":[0.037,0.074]},"magnitude_class":"moderate","notes":"First stationary arrow in GT; the grammar admits it without new primitives (CL-M01 satisfied).","observable":"irreversible flux fraction, entropy production","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":5,"exactness":5,"parameter_robustness":3,"projection_robustness":3,"replication":5},"scope":"GT Round E0A: N=5,6, HELD and FREE, label-covariant O=2 templates incl. two-witness PATH, exact kernels","statement":"Unsaturated two-witness PATH cells (PATHF weak_suppress, PATHH weak_favour) carry a stationary arrow: 9-16% of stationary flux is irreversible, entropy production 0.037-0.074 nats per mean event, projected net current 3-13% of flux.","status":"active","structural_roles":["routing","interaction"],"temporal_character":"stationary"}
{"created_commit":"c31ef92aaf6e5299b9cb15bd7b5c10e768d65f43","created_generation":"GT-E0A","dependence":{"clock":"none","parameters":"weak_favour PATHF and weak_suppress PATHH; N=5 just above floor","projection":"none","scaffold":"both modes"},"epistemic_layer":"OBSERVATION","evidence_refs":["gravity-time/reports/round-e0a-tables.json","gravity-time/reports/gt-e0a-reflection.md"],"finding_id":"GT-F14-SATURATION-HIDES-ARROW","literal_value":{"affinity":2.079,"flux_range":[3e-13,2.9e-11]},"magnitude_class":"zero_within_floor","notes":"Recorded as computed; the expectation is not reworded. X-saturation artefact.","observable":"irreversible flux vs square affinity","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":4,"exactness":5,"parameter_robustness":3,"projection_robustness":4,"replication":5},"scope":"GT Round E0A: N=5,6, HELD and FREE, label-covariant O=2 templates incl. two-witness PATH, exact kernels","statement":"Frozen expectation X4 failed in 4/16 PATH cells: favour-sign PATH at N=6 saturates to the complete graph, so non-gradient rates (max square affinity log 8) carry stationary irreversible flux of only 3e-13 to 3e-11. Rate-level and stationary irreversibility are distinct.","status":"active","structural_roles":["negative_finding","support_boundary"],"temporal_character":"stationary"}
{"created_commit":"c31ef92aaf6e5299b9cb15bd7b5c10e768d65f43","created_generation":"GT-E0A","dependence":{"clock":"event order is clock-free","parameters":"weak grade","projection":"(free-edge count, attachment count)","scaffold":"requires the held source to define slot classes"},"epistemic_layer":"OBSERVATION","evidence_refs":["gravity-time/reports/round-e0a-tables.json","gravity-time/reports/gt-e0a-reflection.md"],"finding_id":"GT-F15-SOURCE-CIRCULATION","literal_value":{"held_asymmetry_range":[0.06,0.1],"pattern_forward":0.0432,"pattern_reverse":0.0166},"magnitude_class":"moderate","notes":"Candidate generic laboratory question: a handover cycle in which an attachment is followed by dissolution of the relation that supported it (CL-Q05 transition-enabling dissolution).","observable":"projected current; event-pair asymmetry","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":4,"exactness":5,"parameter_robustness":3,"projection_robustness":2,"replication":5},"scope":"GT Round E0A: N=5,6, HELD and FREE, label-covariant O=2 templates incl. two-witness PATH, exact kernels","statement":"In HELD, the non-gradient arrow is a source-relative circulation on (free edges, attachments): probe-probe forms, attachment forms, probe-probe dissolves, attachment dissolves; 'form attachment then dissolve adjacent probe-probe' exceeds its time reverse 2.6x (0.043 vs 0.017, N=6).","status":"active","structural_roles":["routing","dissolution_enabler"],"temporal_character":"stationary"}
{"created_commit":"c31ef92aaf6e5299b9cb15bd7b5c10e768d65f43","created_generation":"GT-E0A","dependence":{"clock":"clock-free","parameters":"weak grade","projection":"type and relation only","scaffold":"absent"},"epistemic_layer":"OBSERVATION","evidence_refs":["gravity-time/reports/round-e0a-tables.json","gravity-time/reports/gt-e0a-reflection.md"],"finding_id":"GT-F16-ARROW-PROJECTION-LOSS","literal_value":{"free_asymmetry_range":[0.005,0.0062],"free_flux_range":[0.104,0.142]},"magnitude_class":"small","notes":"Legibility of direction depended on a reference structure; E0B tests an emergent frame.","observable":"event-pair asymmetry vs flux","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":4,"exactness":5,"parameter_robustness":3,"projection_robustness":1,"replication":5},"scope":"GT Round E0A: N=5,6, HELD and FREE, label-covariant O=2 templates incl. two-witness PATH, exact kernels","statement":"In FREE mode the same non-gradient arrow is nearly invisible to class-free event order: pattern asymmetry 0.005-0.006 while irreversible flux is 10-14%.","status":"active","structural_roles":["projection_loss"],"temporal_character":"stationary"}
{"created_commit":"c31ef92aaf6e5299b9cb15bd7b5c10e768d65f43","created_generation":"GT-E0A","dependence":{"clock":"continuous-time law","parameters":"weak grade","projection":"symmetry classes (lossless for label-covariant laws)","scaffold":"both modes"},"epistemic_layer":"OBSERVATION","evidence_refs":["gravity-time/reports/round-e0a-tables.json","gravity-time/reports/gt-e0a-reflection.md"],"finding_id":"GT-F17-EQUAL-RATIO-DIVERGENT-OCCUPANCY","literal_value":{"l1":{"FREE-N5":0.0997,"FREE-N6":0.1716,"HELD-N5":0.181,"HELD-N6":0.3199}},"magnitude_class":"moderate","notes":"Global balance of a non-reversible chain depends on the full rates, not the ratios.","observable":"class-level L1 of pi_ct","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":5,"exactness":5,"parameter_robustness":3,"projection_robustness":4,"replication":5},"scope":"GT Round E0A: N=5,6, HELD and FREE, label-covariant O=2 templates incl. two-witness PATH, exact kernels","statement":"Non-gradient cells with identical local rate ratios (PATHF weak_suppress, PATHH weak_favour) have different stationary laws: class-level L1 0.10 (FREE N5), 0.17 (FREE N6), 0.18 (HELD N5), 0.32 (HELD N6); the gradient kinetic triad differs by <= 1e-14.","status":"active","structural_roles":["occupancy_shift","equivalence"],"temporal_character":"stationary"}
{"created_commit":"c31ef92aaf6e5299b9cb15bd7b5c10e768d65f43","created_generation":"GT-E0A","dependence":{"clock":"both clocks","parameters":"weak grade","projection":"probe distance","scaffold":"HELD"},"epistemic_layer":"OBSERVATION","evidence_refs":["gravity-time/reports/round-e0a-tables.json","gravity-time/reports/gt-e0a-reflection.md"],"finding_id":"GT-F18-ARROW-WITH-REPULSION","literal_value":{"attachment_n6":[0.544,0.638],"detached_range":[0.528,0.551]},"magnitude_class":"large","notes":"Arrow and basin were never observed together in E0A.","observable":"detachment, attachment fraction, rho","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":4,"exactness":5,"parameter_robustness":3,"projection_robustness":3,"replication":5},"scope":"GT Round E0A: N=5,6, HELD and FREE, label-covariant O=2 templates incl. two-witness PATH, exact kernels","statement":"Every unsaturated arrow cell in E0A is an anti-basin: probe detached 53-55% (null 4-7%), attachment fraction 0.54-0.64 against null 0.75 at N=6, near/far activity ratio 1.1-1.4.","status":"active","structural_roles":["occupancy_shift","negative_finding"],"temporal_character":"stationary"}
