{"created_commit":"32ac7f613c44074f8e778845b5830180d2374fa3","created_generation":"GT-E2A","epistemic_layer":"OBSERVATION","evidence_refs":["gravity-time/reports/round-e2a-tables.json","gravity-time/reports/gt-e2-dissolution-analysis.md"],"finding_id":"GT-F49-SOFT-RELEASE-IS-OPPORTUNITY","literal_value":{"opportunity_dominant":170,"opposite_sign":54,"soft_groups":288,"strict":0},"magnitude_class":"moderate","notes":"Matched removal is an instrument, not a modelled intervention.","observable":"matched dissolution: rate, normalisation, jump ratios, passage, precedence","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":4,"exactness":5,"parameter_robustness":3,"projection_robustness":3,"replication":4},"scope":"GT Round E2A: N=5 HELD/FREE and HELD N=6, 21 rule combinations, exact kernels (frozen plan 1974678)","statement":"In soft rules the handover's release step is an opportunity (denominator) effect, not enabling: removing the probe-probe relation leaves the attachment's own dissolution rate unchanged (path_form rules) or lowers it (path_dissolve rules, log ratio -0.02 to -0.17), yet makes it the likelier next event (log +0.29 to +0.64) because a fast competing event is removed; passage within 8 events changes by <= 0.011. Across 288 soft groups: no strict enabling, opportunity larger than rate in 170, next-event change opposite to own-rate change in 54.","status":"active","structural_roles":["negative_finding","dissolution_enabler"],"temporal_character":"finite_horizon_integrated"}
